2d:["$","figure","Robert Knox Sneden’s map of Fox’s and Turner’s Gaps",{"className":"reference-map","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"map-frame static-map-frame","children":["$","a",null,{"className":"map-image-link","href":"/projects/civil-war-field-companion/images/ep185-sneden-south-mountain-map.jpg","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","aria-label":"Open Robert Knox Sneden’s map of Fox’s and Turner’s Gaps at full size","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/projects/civil-war-field-companion/images/ep185-sneden-south-mountain-map.jpg","alt":"Robert Knox Sneden’s hand-drawn color map of the Battle of South Mountain showing Fox’s Gap, Turner’s Gap, Boonsboro, Frosttown, roads, terrain, and troop positions.","width":1600,"height":1200,"loading":"lazy"}]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Robert Knox Sneden’s map of Fox’s and Turner’s Gaps"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Sneden’s wartime map shows South Mountain, the road network, buildings, and colored troop positions between Boonsboro and the Federal approach from the east. Its handwritten notes combine mapping with a retrospective account and casualty totals; it should be read as a participant-era source rather than a modern surveyed battlefield map."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"map-actions","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/projects/civil-war-field-companion/images/ep185-sneden-south-mountain-map.jpg","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Open full-size map ",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$26:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-up-right","size":13}]]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"Library of Congress Geography and Map Division and Virginia Historical Society; see sources below.","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Map source ",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$26:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:ch